WEBVTT

00:00:00.730 --> 00:00:03.350
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:06.260
It's pulling us in!

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.890
Blood Shepherd?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.360
Playmaker!

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.440
The gate is a fake?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.440
It's an excellent copy, on the surface.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.580
It's enitrely different inside.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.550
So someone created it to lure Playmaker?

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.560
I think I know who.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:35.550
Who?

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.790
Don't do anything for now.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.520
Your brother should know it's fake too.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.900
Blood Shepherd?

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.130
Yeah.  I saw him inside the gate.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:54.030
Sorry.  If I only noticed sooner...

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.980
Kusanagi, let's focus on saving Soulburner.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.840
Can you open the gate?

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.080
It doesn't look easy.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.840
Only you can do it, Kusanagi.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.450
Okay.  I'll do my best.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.700
Hey, Playmaker.  They're here.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.370
I'll draw their attention.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.990
The rest's up to you!

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.510
He's not the prey I wanted to catch.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.940
But it's fine.  He has an Ignis too.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.420
Show it to me, Soulburner.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:58.350
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:05.160
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:12.440
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:19.010
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:25.880
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:33.000
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:39.700
I want to share your pain

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.390
That gate was a trap 
created by Blood Shepherd?

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:20.060
To fool your enemies, fool your allies first.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:25.990
I doubt he thinks we're his allies.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.930
Hey!  Two came together!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.390
Playmaker, I know you acted cool, 
saying you’ll draw their attention.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.050
But are you sure?

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.870
We can always log out.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.100
No.  We can’t abandon Soulburner.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.090
How honorable.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:52.040
I guess I have to pitch in and help!

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.590
Releasing the Data Storm!

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:08.440
All right!

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.400
It's up to me!

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.870
Here I come, Playmaker!

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:15.540
I’ll take you on!

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.870
Speed Duel!

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:24.690
Kenmochi and Playmaker have started dueling!

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.090
I’ll go first!  My turn!

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.570
I summon Gouki Suprex!

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:44.280
Due to its effect, I Special 
Summon Gouki Riscorpio!

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.150
A Gouki Deck…

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:53.010
He’s on Go Onizuka’s team after all.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.980
Gouki…  It’s a troubling deck.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:02.450
I send a Gouki monster in my hand to the 
graveyard to Special Summon Gouki Headbatt!

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:11.040
Due to Headbatt’s effect, 
Suprex gains 800 ATK!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.360
Appear!  My circuit!

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.080
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Goukis!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.610
Link Summon!

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:30.000
Appear!  Link 3 Gouki The Blade Ogre!

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.830
A new Gouki monster!

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:38.600
Since three Gouki monsters 
were sent to the graveyard...

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.550
...I add three Gouki cards to my hand!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.800
I activate the spell card, Gouki Re-Match!

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:51.530
I Special Summon Suprex and 
Riscorpio from my graveyard!

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:54.270
Gouki The Blade Ogre’s effect!

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:59.000
For ever monster next to 
its link, it gains 300 ATK!

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.950
I end my turn!

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:07.920
Ooh!  He summoned a powerful-looking Gouki!

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.910
Yeah, you’re right.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:22.830
What's this place?

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:46.350
Blood Shepherd has connected 
into Takeru’s memories.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:51.320
Wake up, Soulburner!  Wake up!

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:06.100
No…  No!

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:28.350
I found your weakness.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.830
Wake up, Soulburner!

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.180
Where am I?

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.700
You're inside Blood Shepherd's trap.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.840
He created that gate.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.290
He analyzed the previous 
gate to create this one.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:54.280
I was fooled too.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:56.360
Blood Shepherd’s trap…

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.710
Come on up, Soulburner.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.840
Learn what’s going on inside that orb yet?

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:25.080
It’s built using a high level 
program, so we can’t access it!

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.650
He decoded an Ignis algorithm?

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:35.290
His intellect rivals Dr. Kogami's.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:39.770
Blood Shepherd is terrifying.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:46.500
Flame told me what you did.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.510
I don’t know what you’re planning.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:54.240
But it's in bad taste to look 
inside my soul without permission!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.230
I'm taking your Ignis.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:11.320
Let me see your skills, Blood Shepherd.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:18.010
What?  An instant kill?

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.480
Duel!

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:34.320
I’ll go first.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:39.040
I summon Duplicate Drone from my hand.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:46.460
Then I activate the Equip Spell, 
Mirror Coat Unit from my hand!

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:54.400
Mirror Coat Unit is an Equip Spell that 
can only be equipped on Drone monsters.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:10:02.640
Effect #1: When it battles a Level 4 or 
lower monster, you take the damage instead.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.650
Effect #2: When the equipped monster 
will be destroyed in battle...

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:14.120
...battle damage becomes 0, and 
this card is destroyed instead.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:18.590
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:25.160
He'll let his AI explain every 
little effect?  So annoying.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:28.840
Ignore it.  Don't let him dictate the pace.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.810
Yeah, I know!

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.920
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:40.450
I discard Salamangreat Parro to 
activate Salamangreat Meer’s effect!

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.690
It Special Summons itself from my hand!

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:49.960
Next, I summon Salamangreat Wolvie!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.980
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:06.180
The summoning conditions are 
two Fire Effect Monsters!

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:10.680
I set Meer and Wolvie in the Link Markers!

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.960
Link Summon!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:19.470
Link 2 Salamangreat Sunlight Wolf!

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.940
My hand's Salamangreat Mole's effect!

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:31.010
When Sunlight Wolf is Link Summoned, 
it Special Summons itself!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:35.140
Sunlight Wolf’s effect!

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:40.110
When a monster is summoned or Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:45.350
...I can return a Salamangreat 
in my graveyard back to my hand!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.260
I’ll keep going!

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:51.180
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:57.100
The summoning conditions are at 
least two Fire Effect Monsters!

00:11:57.100 --> 00:12:03.070
I set Salamangreat Mole and Link 2 
Sunlight Wolf in the Link Markers!

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.000
Link Summon!

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:15.480
Appear!  Link 3 Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.450
Heatleo’s effect!

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:26.430
When it's Link Summoned, I can return one 
card in your Spell & Trap Zone to your deck!

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:30.900
I return the Equip Spell, Mirror Coat Unit!

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:38.410
Mirror Coat Unit’s effect now activates.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.340
Mirror Coat Unit’s Effect #3:

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:42.370
What?

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:47.350
When this card leaves the field, the 
equipped monster returns to the hand.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:52.320
And a copy of that monster is 
added from the deck to the hand.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:56.790
Your AI only explained two effects!

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:59.260
Because I didn’t let it say more.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.630
Be careful, Soulburner.

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.730
This is what he does.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:10.240
I  just checked the data log 
of his duel against Playmaker.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.410
That’s not what it said!

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:17.380
Who decided that an AI's info is accurate?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.030
You made the AI tell a lie?

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.190
Exactly.

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.660
It didn't lie this time.  
I guess that's better.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:31.630
You’re a fool for believing an AI’s info.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.000
What?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.100
An AI is simply a tool that obeys humans.

00:13:36.100 --> 00:13:42.210
If a human says something white 
is black, then it's black.

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:46.620
Since you think of an AI as a partner...

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:50.680
...you'll never understand 
the pain of my right arm.

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.640
Well, whatever.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.890
Because in the end, your field is wide open!

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.850
Now’s my chance-

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.910
Please be careful.

00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:03.090
There’s a chance he 
will attack you directly.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:06.540
Hey, that wasn't a lie.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:10.110
Yeah.  It'll be difficult if 
it mixes the truth with lies.

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:11.330
Yeah.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:15.460
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Drone Barricade!

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:22.770
When this card is in the Spell & Trap Zone, 
your monsters can’t attack me directly.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.850
Watch this!

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:30.210
I activate the Field Spell, 
Salamangreat Sanctuary!

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:35.680
Once per turn, when Link Summoning 
a Salamangreat Link Monster...

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:39.260
...I can Link Summon using 
my field's Salamangreat

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:44.460
Link Monster with the same name 
instead of Link Materials!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:48.700
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:55.410
I set Salamangreat Heatleo 
in the Link Marker!

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:06.320
Reincarnation Link Summon!

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:16.670
Be reborn!  Link 3 Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.410
So this is Reincarnation Link Summon…

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:29.870
Since I Reincarnation Link Summoned, one card 
in your Spell & Trap Zone returns to your deck!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.340
I return Drone Barricade!

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:37.080
The Continuous Trap, Drone 
Barricade’s effect.

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:42.060
When it's the target of an 
effect, I can banish it...

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:51.010
...to set a Drone Barricade from my deck in 
the Spell & Trap Zone and activate it that turn!

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:57.080
He already had a strategy against our deck.

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:01.760
Reincarnating Heatleo isn’t 
a secret technique anymore.

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:05.820
Does that mean I’m famous?

00:16:05.820 --> 00:16:07.730
I end my turn!

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:10.970
My turn.  I draw!

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:16.890
I have all the pieces.

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:21.300
Soulburner, you will lose this turn.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:22.500
What?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.380
But you won't lose against me.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.600
You’re going to lose to yourself.

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:29.570
What do you mean?

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:32.320
You're about to find out.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:38.740
By showing you three copies of 
a Machine-Type in my hand...

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:43.220
...I activate the trap card, 3D Bio Scanner!

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:48.460
I can Special Summon a non-Machine 
monster from my deck!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:51.020
I choose...

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:54.050
Despair from the Dark!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.520
Oh no!  Soulburner’s trauma!

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:23.460
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:27.260
I Special Summon Linkslayer from my hand!

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.980
Then I summon Storm Cipher!

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:41.010
Two monsters with at least 2000 ATK already?

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:44.830
But my Blade Ogre has 3000 ATK!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.420
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.860
The summoning conditions 
are two Effect Monsters!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.520
Link Summon!

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.960
Appear!  Link 2 Pentestag!

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.830
1600 ATK…

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:10.470
Why did he Link Summon a 
monster with lower ATK?

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:17.950
I Special Summon Link Infra-Flier from 
my hand next to Pentestag’s link!

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:24.410
What?  A monster with 0 ATK?

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.660
What's he planning?

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:32.770
I equip the Equip Spell, Cyberse 
Annihilation on Pentestag!

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:39.370
When equipped with Cyberse Annihilation, my 
monster's ATK

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.970
become the same as the monster it battles!

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:46.200
He’s going for mutual 
destruction with Blade Ogre!

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:49.180
Finish this, Playmaker!

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:50.710
Battle!

00:18:50.710 --> 00:18:55.690
Pentestag attacks Gouki Riscorpio!

00:18:56.140 --> 00:19:00.920
Instead of Blade Ogre, he's attacking 
Riscorpio that’s in defense?

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:10.090
Pentestag’s effect!

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:19.720
When a linked monster attacks a monster in 
defense position, it deals piercing damage!

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:20.840
What?

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:26.310
Cyberse Annihilation’s effect activates!

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:31.280
You take damage equal to the 
destroyed monster’s ATK!

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:34.620
Riscorpio has...

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.290
2300 ATK!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.490
You got served!

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.240
Kusanagi!  How’s the rescue program?

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:51.670
Working on it!

00:19:53.640 --> 00:19:58.490
The Ignis program is built 
using a special algorithm.

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:03.860
It's incredible that he decoded 
it and created this trap.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:06.860
Giving up, Kusanagi?

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:10.050
Who do you think I am?

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:15.030
I'll solve this trap and rescue Soulburner!

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:17.760
I’m counting on you, Kusanagi!

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.970
Here's another one!

00:20:21.970 --> 00:20:23.300
Let's go!

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:37.070
I knew it.

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.860
I summon Duplicate Drone from my hand!

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:47.300
The effects of two Duplicate 
Drones in my hand!

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:53.030
When there’s a monster on my field with 
the same name, they Special Summon themselves.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:21:04.080
Once per turn, I can treat a non-Machine 
monster on my field as a Continuous Spell...

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:06.780
...and place it in the Spell & Trap Zone.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:11.480
I select Despair from the Dark!

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:19.670
And Duplicate Drone is treated as 
the same monster as the target!

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:40.520
Taking advantage of his 
trauma?  That's not fair!

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:44.380
I'll do anything to fulfill my goal.

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:48.490
Especially when my opponent relies on an AI.

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:53.460
I'll bury you in dark despair.

00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:26.530
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:33.110
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:36.610
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:36.610 --> 00:22:39.750
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:44.500
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:47.320
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:58.190
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:01.340
With repeating "nows"

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:05.260
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:11.240
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:14.520
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:44.520
Blood Shepherd makes a cruel decision: 
It's time to end his prey.

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:49.890
When the final merciless strike 
swings down on Soulburner...

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:53.730
...a small flame appears in his eyes.

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:58.370
Stand up, Takeru!  Now's 
the time to reincarnate!

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:02.640
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Reincarnating Flame

00:24:02.640 --> 00:24:05.050
Into the VRAINS!
